[size=4][b]A compass bar across the top of the screen, with your map pins on it at their real bearing.[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]A pin at your two o'clock appears at your two o'clock. Read straight from the in-game map, with the same icons.[/*]
[*]Icons grow and brighten as you close on them.[/*]
[*]The pin nearest the centre shows its name and distance. One at a time, not a wall of overlapping text.[/*]
[*]A clock above the bar names the part of the day - Dawn 42 - 6:40 AM, Night 43 - 12:15 AM - so you know whether it is safe out without doing the arithmetic.[/*]
[*]Hides itself while the map, your inventory or the game menu is open.[/*]
[*]Pins you have ticked off do not show, and nor do emptied chests if you also run Cartur's Map Pins.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Config[/b][/size]

BepInEx/config/com.jekkle.valheim.carturcompassandclock.cfg, written on first run. Changes apply live - no restart needed.

[list]
[*][b]PinRange[/b] (300) - metres. Pins further out do not show.[/*]
[*][b]FieldOfView[/b] (90) - degrees of heading visible across the bar.[/*]
[*][b]ShowPinNames[/b] (true) - name and distance of the centred pin.[/*]
[*][b]TwelveHourClock[/b] (true) - 1:05 PM. Off gives 13:05.[/*]
[*][b]FrameWidth[/b] (657) - bar width, on a 1920x1080 basis. Scales with your resolution.[/*]
[*][b]FrameOffsetX[/b] (0) - distance right of screen centre. Negative moves it left.[/*]
[*][b]FrameOffsetY[/b] (54) - gap from the top of the screen down to the bar.[/*]
[*][b]EditMode[/b] (false) - drag the compass around the screen. See below.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Moving and resizing it[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Turn on EditMode.[/*]
[*][b]Open your inventory[/b], so you have a free cursor - without a menu open the mouse is driving the camera.[/*]
[*]Drag the box to move it. Drag the grip on its right edge to resize it.[/*]
[*]Turn EditMode back off.[/*]
[/list]

Where you drop it is written straight back to FrameWidth, FrameOffsetX and FrameOffsetY, so it survives restarts and you can still fine-tune the numbers by hand.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

No Harmony patches - the compass is its own UI canvas that reads the map's pin list. It does not touch the map, the HUD, or anyone else's UI.

Single-player and multiplayer, client-side only. The server does not need it, and other players do not need it.

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Requires BepInEx. Unpack into your Valheim folder so the DLL lands in BepInEx/plugins.

